; RELATIONS ON A SET
;
; The scene of the exercises on relations: with set.kurt, a relation R on a set A is a set of
; pairs, and `(x, y) ∈ R` says that x is in relation R to y (often written x R y, or x ~ y, or
; x ≤ y). Only reflexivity depends on the set A; the other properties are about the pairs in R.
;
;     (x, y) ∈ R              x is related to y
;     reflexive(R, A)         every x ∈ A is related to itself
;     symmetric(R)            x related to y gives y related to x
;     transitive(R)           x related to y and y related to z give x related to z
;     antisymmetric(R)        x related to y and y related to x give x = y
;     equivalence(R, A)       R is an equivalence relation on A
;     order(R, A)             R is a partial order on A
;     class(a, R, A)          the equivalence class [a] of a: the y ∈ A with a related to y
;
; From set.kurt: `x ∈ A`, `A ⊂ B`, `A ∩ B`, `A ∪ B`, `∅`, `{x ∈ A | P(x)}`; from equality.kurt
; `x ≠ y`.
;
; The rules (with set.kurt, and with it propositional.kurt, logic.kurt and equality.kurt):
;
;     "reflexive"       reflexive(R, A) ⇔ ∀ x ∈ A ((x, x) ∈ R)
;     "symmetric"       symmetric(R) ⇔ ∀ x ∀ y ((x, y) ∈ R ⇒ (y, x) ∈ R)
;     "transitive"      transitive(R) ⇔ ∀ x ∀ y ∀ z ((x, y) ∈ R ∧ (y, z) ∈ R ⇒ (x, z) ∈ R)
;     "antisymmetric"   antisymmetric(R) ⇔ ∀ x ∀ y ((x, y) ∈ R ∧ (y, x) ∈ R ⇒ x = y)
;     "equivalence"     equivalence(R, A) ⇔ reflexive(R, A) ∧ symmetric(R) ∧ transitive(R)
;     "order"           order(R, A) ⇔ reflexive(R, A) ∧ antisymmetric(R) ∧ transitive(R)
;     "class"           class(a, R, A) = {y ∈ A | (a, y) ∈ R}
;
; and from set.kurt (the ones you will need most):
;
;     "extensionality"    A = B ⇔ ∀ c (c ∈ A ⇔ c ∈ B)
;     "subset"            A ⊂ B ⇔ ∀ c (c ∈ A ⇒ c ∈ B)
;     "separation"        a ∈ {x ∈ A | P(x)} ⇔ a ∈ A ∧ P(a)
;     "in-intersection"   c ∈ A ∩ B ⇔ c ∈ A ∧ c ∈ B
;     "empty-set"         ¬(c ∈ ∅)
;
; This file is the scene of the exercises: they load it with `load theory/relations`. Don't
; change it.
load set

arity reflexive (_, _), symmetric 1, transitive 1, antisymmetric 1, equivalence (_, _), order (_, _), class (_, _, _)
prop reflexive 0, symmetric 0, transitive 0, antisymmetric 0, equivalence 0, order 0

def reflexive($R, $A) ⇔ ∀ x ∈ $A ((x, x) ∈ $R)                                     "reflexive"
def symmetric($R) ⇔ ∀ x ∀ y ((x, y) ∈ $R ⇒ (y, x) ∈ $R)                            "symmetric"
def transitive($R) ⇔ ∀ x ∀ y ∀ z ((x, y) ∈ $R ∧ (y, z) ∈ $R ⇒ (x, z) ∈ $R)         "transitive"
def antisymmetric($R) ⇔ ∀ x ∀ y ((x, y) ∈ $R ∧ (y, x) ∈ $R ⇒ x = y)                "antisymmetric"
def equivalence($R, $A) ⇔ reflexive($R, $A) ∧ symmetric($R) ∧ transitive($R)      "equivalence"
def order($R, $A) ⇔ reflexive($R, $A) ∧ antisymmetric($R) ∧ transitive($R)        "order"
def class($a, $R, $A) = {y ∈ $A | ($a, y) ∈ $R}                                     "class"
